Welcome to the final part of Making Dondurma Turkish Stretchy Ice Cream at home. This is it, this is the way. I've tried other recipes and this is THE recipe to use to make correct texture, correct stretchy, just basically correct dondurma turkish ice cream.
Is this Dondurma super luxury.....YES
Is this Turkish Ice Cream easy to make......YES
Is this Dondurma super stretchy........YES
Are you going to love the artistic element of it.......YES
Have is said YES too many time.........NO..... 😉

FROM THIS VIDEO ONWARDS, THE RECIPES WILL BE IN THE VIDEOS THEMSELVES AND ALSO ON MY PATREON AND KO-FI PAGES. IT TAKES TOO MUCH TO MAKE ALL THESE VIDEOS FOR NOTHING. 

SO FOR THIS DONDURMA TURKISH ICE CREAM YOU WILL NEED:
450g Milk at 2% fat (1 + 3/4 cups)
350g Cream at 33-36% fat (1 + 1/4 cup + 2 tbsp)
120g Sugar (1/2 cup + 1 tbsp)
40g Dextrose (or 50g additional sugar)(1/4 cup)
40g SMP (2tbsp + 1 tsp)
4g Glucomannan (1 tsp) Available on Amazon everywhere (Also called Konjac Root Flour)

